# Portfolio site

A single-page, vanilla HTML/CSS/JS portfolio that pulls your GitHub repos live
and animates everything with [Anime.js](https://animejs.com/). No build step —
just open `index.html` in a browser.

## Files

| File | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `index.html` | Page structure |
| `styles.css` | All styling, including the color/font design tokens |
| `script.js` | GitHub fetch, animations, modals, dark mode, form validation |
| `projects.json` | Optional: attach a video demo / custom copy to specific repos |
| `README.md` | This file |

## 1. Set your GitHub username

Open `script.js` and change the first line:

```js
const GITHUB_USERNAME = "YOUR_GITHUB_USERNAME"; // <-- change this
```

The site fetches `https://api.github.com/users/<username>/repos?sort=updated&per_page=100`,
drops forks and repos with no description, sorts what's left by star count, and
shows the top 6. Results are cached in `localStorage` for 1 hour so repeat
visits don't hit GitHub's (unauthenticated) rate limit of 60 requests/hour.

## 2. Add video demos (optional)

Edit `projects.json`. Key each entry by the exact repo name:

```json
{
  "my-cool-app": {
    "videoId": "dQw4w9WgXcQ",
    "description": "Optional override for the card/modal description.",
    "stack": ["React", "Node.js", "PostgreSQL"]
  }
}
```

- `videoId` is the part of a YouTube URL after `watch?v=`. Any repo with a
  `videoId` gets a "Watch demo" button that opens an embedded player in a modal.
- `description` and `stack` are optional — if omitted, the card falls back to
  the repo's GitHub description and primary language.
- Repos not listed in `projects.json` still display fine, just without a video.

If `projects.json` is missing (or blocked, e.g. when opening `index.html`
directly via `file://` in some browsers), the site silently falls back to
GitHub-only data.

## 3. Replace placeholder content

Search `index.html` for:
- **Bio paragraphs** in the About section
- **Social links** in the nav — add your LinkedIn / Twitter URLs (a commented-out
  example sits next to the GitHub link)
- **Résumé entries** in the résumé modal at the bottom of the file (add your
  school, dates and any internships)
- **Photo** — `MYPHOTO.jpeg`
- The About stats, language chips, "currently building" panel and heatmap are
  **filled in live from GitHub** — nothing to edit there.
- For link previews when you share the site, add an absolute `og:image` URL in
  the `<head>` after you deploy (there's a comment showing where).

## 4. Colors & fonts

Everything lives in CSS custom properties at the top of `styles.css`:

```css
:root {
  --bg: #0b0d10;
  --accent: #e8823a;
  --font-head: "Space Grotesk", "Inter", sans-serif;
  --font-body: "Inter", sans-serif;
  ...
}
```

Change these tokens to restyle the whole site. (There is no light theme — the
site is dark only.)

## 5. Contact form

The form validates client-side (name required, valid email pattern, message
length). To make it actually send, create a free endpoint at Formspree, Getform
or Web3Forms and paste its URL into `FORM_ENDPOINT` near the top of `script.js`:

```js
const FORM_ENDPOINT = "https://formspree.io/f/xxxxxxx";
```

While `FORM_ENDPOINT` is empty, the form tells visitors it isn't connected yet
instead of pretending the message was sent.

## 6. Deploying

Since there's no build step, you can drop these files straight onto GitHub
Pages, Netlify, Vercel, or any static host. Just make sure `projects.json`
gets served alongside `index.html` (i.e. don't rename or move it without
updating the `fetch("projects.json")` call in `script.js`).

## 7. Galaxy, command palette & terminal

- **Galaxy** (`initHeroGalaxy` in `script.js`): one fixed WebGL layer behind every
  page. On Home you can drag to rotate, scroll/pinch to zoom, double-click to
  reset. Leaving Home flies the camera into it; on other pages it dims and drifts.
  Hovering a project card tints it with that repo's language colour and speeds it
  up. Tunables are at the top of the function (`DIST_DEFAULT`, `BG_DIST`,
  `PARTICLES`, ...). The old F1-car background is kept in the HTML but no longer
  started — uncomment `initF1Car()` and remove the `.site-bg { display: none }`
  rule to bring it back.
- **Command palette:** `Ctrl/⌘ + K` anywhere — jump to pages, open projects,
  open the résumé, reset the galaxy.
- **Terminal** on the About page: `help`, `whoami`, `ls`, `open <project>`,
  `skills`, `git log`, `goto <page>`, `galaxy reset|warp`, `clear`. Edit the
  `whoami` text in `initTerminal()` in `script.js`.
- **GitHub panel:** latest commit + a 13-week activity heatmap from GitHub's
  public events feed. It only sees *public* activity, and GitHub only exposes
  recent events, so very old days show as dashed "unknown" cells.

## Notes

- Respects `prefers-reduced-motion`: entrance/scroll animations are skipped
  and content just appears in place.
- GitHub responses are cached in `localStorage` (repos 1 h, activity 30 min).
- "Download PDF" on the résumé modal uses `window.print()` — most browsers'
  print dialog has a "Save as PDF" destination, which keeps this dependency-free.